## Hardware Script Standard Library - Generic Profile
## Purpose: Default profile with conservative bridge rules for prototyping
## Status: Phase 3 - Standard Library Implementation (BRIDGE-IMPLEMENTATION.md)

#[
GENERIC PROFILE OVERVIEW:

This profile provides sensible defaults for prototyping when no specific
foundry profile is available. It uses "Generic" bridge materials with
conservative properties that work across multiple application domains.

DESIGN PHILOSOPHY:
- Conservative constraints (wide traces, large vias)
- Generic bridge materials (average properties)
- Works for both PCB and IC prototyping
- Educational - shows all bridge types clearly
- Safe defaults - won't violate physics

USAGE:
import @std/profiles/generic

space my_design:
    route power to ground  # Uses Generic_Silicide + Generic_Via_Fill

BRIDGE PRIORITY STACK:
1. Explicit user override (highest)
2. This profile's bridge rules
3. Fallback to error (no implicit bridges)

See: BRIDGE-IMPLEMENTATION.md Section 3 (Priority Stack)
]#

## ============================================================================
## GENERIC PROFILE - Conservative Defaults for Prototyping
## ============================================================================

profile Generic:
    description: "Generic profile with conservative constraints for prototyping"
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## LAYER CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    layer:
        max_count: 6                          # Support up to 6 layers
        min_thickness: 1.6mm                  # Standard PCB thickness
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## TRACE CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    trace:
        min_width: 200µm                      # Conservative 8mil traces
        min_spacing: 200µm                    # Conservative 8mil spacing
        max_width: 10mm                       # Power planes
        max_length: 1m                        # Reasonable board size
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## VIA CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    via:
        min_diameter: 400µm                   # Conservative via size
        min_annular_ring: 200µm               # Large annular ring
        max_aspect_ratio: 10                  # Depth/diameter ratio
        default_via_fill: Generic_Via_Fill    # Default fill material
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## CLEARANCE CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    clearance:
        high_voltage: 3mm                     # Conservative HV clearance
        safety_factor: 2.5                    # Extra safety margin
        low_voltage_threshold: 50V
        medium_voltage_threshold: 150V
        high_voltage_threshold: 300V
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## THERMAL CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    thermal:
        ambient_temp: 25C                     # Room temperature
        max_operating_temp: 85C               # Standard commercial range
        max_temp_rise: 20C                    # Conservative temp rise
        clustering_threshold: 5mm             # Via clustering distance
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## MANUFACTURING CONSTRAINTS
    ## ========================================================================
    
    manufacturing:
        copper_thickness: 35µm                # 1oz copper
        ipc2221_k_external: 0.048             # IPC-2221 constants
        ipc2221_k_internal: 0.024
        min_feature_size: 100µm               # Conservative minimum
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## STACKUP DEFINITION
    ## ========================================================================
    
    stackup:
        dielectric_height: 200µm              # Inter-layer spacing
        dielectric_material: "FR4"            # Standard PCB material
        copper_thickness: 35µm                # 1oz copper
        default_impedance: 50.0               # Standard impedance
    
    ## ========================================================================
    ## BRIDGE RULES - Material Transition Mappings
    ## ========================================================================
    
    ## Silicon-to-Metal Bridges (IC Fabrication)
    ## Used when routing from silicon layers to metal layers
    
    bridge Silicon to Metal:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Generic_Via_Fill
    
    bridge Silicon_N to Metal:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Generic_Via_Fill
    
    bridge Silicon_P to Metal:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Generic_Via_Fill
    
    bridge Silicon to Copper:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    bridge Silicon to Aluminum:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    bridge Polysilicon to Metal:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Generic_Via_Fill
    
    ## Metal-to-Metal Bridges (Inter-layer Vias)
    ## Used for standard via connections between metal layers
    
    bridge Metal to Metal:
        interface: Generic_Barrier
        thickness: 20nm
        fill: Generic_Via_Fill
    
    bridge Copper to Copper:
        interface: Generic_Barrier
        thickness: 10nm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Aluminum to Aluminum:
        interface: Generic_Barrier
        thickness: 20nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    bridge Copper to Aluminum:
        interface: Tungsten_Barrier
        thickness: 20nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    ## Die-to-Die Bridges (3D Integration)
    ## Used for chiplet interconnects and 3D stacking
    
    bridge Die to Die:
        interface: Generic_Gold_Bump
        thickness: 5µm
        fill: Gold
    
    bridge Silicon to Silicon:
        interface: Generic_Gold_Bump
        thickness: 5µm
        fill: Gold
    
    bridge Chip to Chip:
        interface: Generic_Gold_Bump
        thickness: 5µm
        fill: Gold
    
    ## PCB-to-Component Bridges (Board Assembly)
    ## Used for component mounting and through-hole connections
    
    bridge PCB to Component:
        interface: Generic_Solder
        thickness: 100µm
        fill: Generic_Solder
    
    bridge Copper to Pad:
        interface: Generic_Solder
        thickness: 100µm
        fill: Generic_Solder
    
    bridge Trace to Pin:
        interface: Generic_Solder
        thickness: 100µm
        fill: Generic_Solder
    
    ## Substrate Bridges (Backside Connections)
    ## Used for substrate contacts and backside metallization
    
    bridge Silicon to Substrate:
        interface: Generic_Silicide
        thickness: 100nm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Die to Package:
        interface: Generic_Solder
        thickness: 50µm
        fill: Generic_Solder

## ============================================================================
## GENERIC PROFILE VARIANTS - Domain-Specific Defaults
## ============================================================================

profile Generic_IC:
    description: "Generic IC profile - silicon fabrication defaults"
    
    layer:
        max_count: 10                         # More metal layers for ICs
        min_thickness: 500µm                  # Silicon wafer
    
    trace:
        min_width: 100nm                      # Nanometer-scale features
        min_spacing: 100nm
    
    via:
        min_diameter: 200nm                   # Nanoscale vias
        min_annular_ring: 50nm
        default_via_fill: Tungsten            # Standard IC via fill
    
    manufacturing:
        min_feature_size: 100nm               # Sub-micron features
    
    ## IC-specific bridge rules
    
    bridge Silicon_N to Copper:
        interface: Cobalt_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    bridge Silicon_P to Copper:
        interface: Cobalt_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Tungsten
    
    bridge Copper to Copper:
        interface: Tantalum_Nitride
        thickness: 5nm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Polysilicon to Metal:
        interface: Titanium_Silicide
        thickness: 50nm
        fill: Tungsten

profile Generic_PCB:
    description: "Generic PCB profile - board fabrication defaults"
    
    layer:
        max_count: 6
        min_thickness: 1.6mm
    
    trace:
        min_width: 200µm                      # 8mil traces
        min_spacing: 200µm
    
    via:
        min_diameter: 400µm
        min_annular_ring: 200µm
        default_via_fill: Copper              # Plated through-hole
    
    manufacturing:
        copper_thickness: 35µm                # 1oz copper
        min_feature_size: 200µm
    
    stackup:
        dielectric_material: "FR4"
        copper_thickness: 35µm
    
    ## PCB-specific bridge rules
    
    bridge Copper to Copper:
        interface: Copper                     # Direct plating
        thickness: 35µm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Copper to Pad:
        interface: SAC305_Solder
        thickness: 100µm
        fill: SAC305_Solder
    
    bridge Trace to Component:
        interface: SAC305_Solder
        thickness: 100µm
        fill: SAC305_Solder

profile Generic_3D:
    description: "Generic 3D profile - chiplet and TSV defaults"
    
    layer:
        max_count: 20                         # Multiple die stacks
        min_thickness: 50µm                   # Thinned silicon
    
    via:
        min_diameter: 5µm                     # TSV diameter
        min_annular_ring: 2µm
        max_aspect_ratio: 20                  # High aspect ratio TSVs
        default_via_fill: Copper              # TSV fill
    
    manufacturing:
        min_feature_size: 1µm                 # TSV features
    
    ## 3D-specific bridge rules
    
    bridge Silicon to Silicon:
        interface: Micro_Bump
        thickness: 15µm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Die to Die:
        interface: Micro_Bump
        thickness: 15µm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge TSV to Metal:
        interface: Tantalum_Nitride           # TSV liner
        thickness: 10nm
        fill: Copper

profile Generic_Package:
    description: "Generic package profile - flip-chip and BGA defaults"
    
    layer:
        max_count: 4                          # Package substrate
        min_thickness: 400µm
    
    via:
        min_diameter: 100µm
        min_annular_ring: 50µm
        default_via_fill: Copper
    
    ## Package-specific bridge rules
    
    bridge Die to Package:
        interface: Copper_Pillar
        thickness: 60µm
        fill: Copper
    
    bridge Package to PCB:
        interface: SAC305_Solder
        thickness: 500µm                      # BGA ball height
        fill: SAC305_Solder
    
    bridge Chip to Substrate:
        interface: Copper_Pillar
        thickness: 60µm
        fill: Copper

## ============================================================================
## MATERIAL ALIASES - Convenience Names
## ============================================================================

#[
Material aliases allow users to use common names that map to specific materials.
This improves code readability and matches industry terminology.

Example:
    bridge Silicon to M1:  # M1 is aliased to Copper
        interface: Cobalt_Silicide
]#

material_alias M1: Copper
material_alias M2: Copper
material_alias M3: Copper
material_alias M4: Copper
material_alias M5: Copper
material_alias M6: Copper
material_alias M7: Aluminum
material_alias M8: Aluminum

material_alias Metal1: Copper
material_alias Metal2: Copper
material_alias Metal3: Copper
material_alias Metal4: Copper

material_alias Poly: Polysilicon
material_alias Gate: Polysilicon

material_alias N_Plus: Silicon_N
material_alias P_Plus: Silicon_P
material_alias N_Well: Silicon_N
material_alias P_Well: Silicon_P

material_alias Via_Fill: Generic_Via_Fill
material_alias Contact_Fill: Tungsten

material_alias Solder: SAC305_Solder
material_alias Lead_Free: SAC305_Solder
material_alias Leaded: SnPb_Eutectic

material_alias Bump: Generic_Gold_Bump
material_alias C4: Solder_Bump_C4

## ============================================================================
## USAGE EXAMPLES
## ============================================================================

#[
EXAMPLE 1: Basic IC Routing (Router Level - Automatic)

import @std/profiles/generic

space my_chip:
    route M1.source to GND
    # Compiler automatically:
    # 1. Detects Silicon → Copper transition
    # 2. Looks up: bridge Silicon to Copper
    # 3. Inserts Generic_Silicide (50nm) + Tungsten fill

EXAMPLE 2: Manual Assembly (Assembly Level - Explicit)

import @std/profiles/generic

space my_chip:
    add pour(Silicon_N) on z:1
    
    # User MUST explicitly add bridge
    add contact(Generic_Silicide) at [50µm, 50µm] spanning z:2 to z:2:
        diameter: 500nm
    
    add contact(Tungsten) at [50µm, 50µm] spanning z:3 to z:5:
        diameter: 500nm
    
    add pour(Copper) on z:6

EXAMPLE 3: Override Bridge Material

import @std/profiles/generic

space my_chip:
    route M1.source to GND:
        bridge: Cobalt_Silicide  # Override Generic_Silicide

EXAMPLE 4: PCB Assembly

import @std/profiles/generic_pcb

space my_board:
    route power_trace to component_pad
    # Uses SAC305_Solder bridge automatically

EXAMPLE 5: 3D Chiplet

import @std/profiles/generic_3d

space my_chiplet:
    route die1.signal to die2.signal
    # Uses Micro_Bump bridge automatically

See: BRIDGE-IMPLEMENTATION.md Section 9 (User Experience Examples)
]#

## ============================================================================
## END OF GENERIC PROFILE
## ============================================================================
